---
import "../styles/global.css";
import InfoPage from "../components/InfoPage.astro";
---
<InfoPage title="Data controls that are yours." eyebrow="Local-first by design" description="A clear, browser-based way to keep, move, or remove your Gym & Tonic week.">
  <section class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3"><article class="border-t-2 border-[var(--sage)] pt-5"><p class="font-display text-3xl">01</p><h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Download</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">Save a JSON backup of your current plan, preferences, completions, reflections, and active workout progress.</p></article><article class="border-t-2 border-[var(--terra)] pt-5"><p class="font-display text-3xl">02</p><h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Restore</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">Bring back a valid Gym &amp; Tonic backup. Invalid files are rejected before they can replace your current week.</p></article><article class="border-t-2 border-[var(--ink)] pt-5"><p class="font-display text-3xl">03</p><h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Delete</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">Remove planner data, saved templates, history, reflections, and workout progress from this browser after an explicit confirmation.</p></article></section>
  <section class="mt-12 rounded-[1.5rem] bg-[var(--ink)] p-6 text-white sm:p-8"><p class="eyebrow text-[#f2b36f]">Before you switch devices</p><h2 class="mt-3 max-w-xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold">Export first. Local means no automatic cross-device sync.</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-7 text-white/70">Gym &amp; Tonic does not use an account or cloud backup. Download your plan before clearing browser data, changing browsers, or moving to another device.</p><a href="/plan" class="button-primary mt-6 inline-block bg-white text-[var(--sage-deep)] hover:bg-[var(--surface-subtle)]">Open Data controls</a></section>
</InfoPage>
